1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,350
Elias's paper had his obituary.

2
00:00:02,820 --> 00:00:05,070
It arrived a day
early: his name,

3
00:00:05,260 --> 00:00:07,510
his apartment, a fire at 3:07.

4
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:09,030
He was alive.

5
00:00:10,266 --> 00:00:11,196
He had no subscription.

6
00:00:11,196 --> 00:00:14,516
Underneath, in small
print: one name per

7
00:00:14,516 --> 00:00:18,215
fire. At 2:40,
Elias knocked on 4A.

8
00:00:18,865 --> 00:00:20,815
Mara's heater had been
sparking all week.

9
00:00:21,125 --> 00:00:22,435
She'd asked him to fix it.

10
00:00:22,725 --> 00:00:24,055
He told her to call the super.

11
00:00:24,525 --> 00:00:26,075
He took the stairs
and didn't look

12
00:00:26,075 --> 00:00:28,395
back. From the
hotel, he watched the

13
00:00:28,395 --> 00:00:29,235
smoke rise.

14
00:00:29,905 --> 00:00:32,015
At 3:07, 4B burned.

15
00:00:32,645 --> 00:00:34,155
The next paper
waited at the front

16
00:00:34,155 --> 00:00:36,035
desk. Same fire.

17
00:00:36,305 --> 00:00:37,075
Same hour.

18
00:00:37,265 --> 00:00:38,015
Different name.

19
00:00:39,155 --> 00:00:40,185
Mara Kwan.

20
00:00:40,185 --> 00:00:41,445
Apartment 4A.

21
00:00:41,655 --> 00:00:43,525
It said she'd entered 4B to warn

22
00:00:43,525 --> 00:00:46,185
him. Elias laid the
two obituaries side

23
00:00:46,185 --> 00:00:47,145
by side.

24
00:00:47,475 --> 00:00:48,125
His name.

25
00:00:48,315 --> 00:00:51,966
Mara's. The paper wasn't
predicting the future.

26
00:00:52,416 --> 00:00:54,366
It was choosing who paid for it.
